+# Second-operator onboarding
+
+A step-by-step path for an operator who starts using Curator, a managed-home
+profile, and `curator run` on their own machine. Every command below was run
+on a clean HOME (macOS, Curator built from trunk, curator-run 0.1.0, stub
+`claude`/`codex` executables). Real agents and Linux were not exercised; see
+[Unverified](#unverified).
+
+## 1. Prerequisites
+
+- macOS or Linux, `git` on `PATH`.
+- `gh` (with `gh attestation verify`) or `cosign`, for the verified installer.
+- Go toolchain from the launcher's `go.mod`, for `curator-run`.
+- The agent tools you use (`claude`, `codex`) on `PATH`, logged in natively
+  once (`claude` then `/login`; `codex login`).
+
+## 2. Install Curator and the launcher
+
+```bash
+brew install relux-works/tap/curator
+# or the verified installer:
+curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/relux-works/curator/main/install.sh | sh
+```
+
+The installer verifies `checksums.txt` with `gh attestation verify` or, if
+`gh` is missing, with the release's keyless cosign signature, and then
+checks the archive's SHA-256. It refuses to install when neither verifier is
+available. Use `CURATOR_INSTALL_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY=1` only in an emergency:
+it installs the executable with no integrity check. `CURATOR_VERSION` pins a
+release and `CURATOR_BIN_DIR` picks the directory (default `/usr/local/bin`,
+fallback `~/.local/bin`).
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/relux-works/curator-agent-launcher/cmd/curator-run@v0.1.0
+```
+
+Put `$(go env GOPATH)/bin` (or a dedicated `GOBIN`) on `PATH`. Do not install
+`curator-run` into `~/.local/bin` or under `~/.curator/environments`.
+Umbrella discovery refuses those locations with `subcommand_provider_untrusted`.
+
+## 3. Machine initialization
+
+```bash
+curator bootstrap --if-missing --non-interactive \
+  --skills-root ~/skills --default-agents claude_code,codex_cli
+curator global init
+```
+
+`--skills-root` is required when you pass `--non-interactive`. `curator global init` and every
+`profile`/`env` command fail with `global config not found` until
+`bootstrap` has written `~/.curator/config.json`.
+
+## 4. Managed-home profile
+
+A profile is a git repository or local directory that has an
+`agent-context.json` file at its root:
+
+```json
+{"schema_version": 1, "name": "myprofile", "version": "1.0.0",
+ "context": {"modules": [{"path": "a.md"}]}}
+```
+
+The modules are stored under `context/`, for example `context/a.md`. Install it and make it current:
+
+```bash
+curator profile install /path/to/profile --as myprofile --use   # local path
+curator profile install <git-url> --tag v1.0.0 --as myprofile --use
+curator profile list
+```
+
+A local path takes no `--tag/--range/--revision`, because it is refused with
+`profile_install_ref_conflict`. `--use` also switches the native homes
+(`~/.claude`, `~/.codex`, `~/.config/opencode`, `~/.pi`). It writes
+a marker and the rendered root context there.
+
+Provision and inspect the managed homes:
+
+```bash
+curator env resolve claude_code --repair --format json
+curator env resolve codex_cli --repair --format json
+curator env status
+```
+
+Without `--repair`, the first `env resolve` exits 1 with
+`environment_home_stale: home unprovisioned`. The homes live at
+`~/.curator/environments/<profile>/<env-id>`, and the fragment exports
+`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` or `CODEX_HOME` pointing there.
+
+## 5. Credential passthrough
+
+Managed homes never copy credentials. They either link to the native store
+or rely on a store that is outside the filesystem. The per-tool facts come from
+`internal/envregistry/envregistry.go` (Claude `:240-243`, Codex `:263-265`,
+Pi `:317`), and `effectivePassthrough` applies them
+(`internal/envprofile/managed.go:545-575`).
+
+| Tool | macOS | Linux | What the operator does once |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Claude Code | Nothing linked (`darwin: {}`). Claude keys its Keychain item per `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` (service suffix sha256[0:8]), so the managed home has its own login (`per-home-keychain`, `managed.go:581-587`). | `.credentials.json` symlinked to `~/.claude/.credentials.json` (`file-link`). | macOS: run `/login` once inside each managed home, for example with the first `curator run claude`. Linux: log in natively once. |
+| Codex CLI | `auth.json` symlinked to `~/.codex/auth.json` when the native store is `file` (the default). When `~/.codex/config.toml` sets `cli_auth_credentials_store = "keyring"`, nothing is linked and the keyring is shared ambiently (`managed.go:559-567`). | Same | `codex login` natively once. |
+| Pi | `auth.json` linked to `~/.pi/agent/auth.json` | Same | Log in natively once. |
+
+What was observed on the walk (macOS): `codex_cli/auth.json ->
+~/.codex/auth.json` was a symlink, and the marker recorded
+`strategy keyring-preferred, backend file`. The `claude_code` home had no
+credential entry, and the fake native `~/.claude/.credentials.json` was not
+linked or copied. `env unmanage` and `profile remove` left both native
+credential files byte-identical. An isolated profile links nothing.
+
+## 6. `curator run`
+
+```bash
+curator run claude -- --print hello          # current profile
+curator run codex --profile myprofile -- exec hi
+```
+
+The launcher calls `curator env resolve <env> --repair --format json` and
+then execs the tool with the fragment's `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`/`CODEX_HOME`, the
+lineup model and effort flags, and your arguments after `--`. The walk's stubs
+received `--model claude-opus-5-5 --effort high --print hello`
+and `-m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort="max" exec hi`, the caller's
+cwd, and the full inherited environment.
+
+## 7. Update and removal
+
+```bash
+curator profile update myprofile
+curator env unmanage --restore-backups
+curator profile use default
+curator profile remove myprofile     # refused (profile_in_use) while current
+```
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+| Symptom | Fix |
+|---|---|
+| `global config not found: ~/.curator/config.json` | Run `curator bootstrap` first (step 3). |
+| `bootstrap requires --skills-root` | Pass `--skills-root <dir>`. |
+| `profile_install_ref_conflict` | Drop `--tag/--range/--revision` for a local path. |
+| `environment_home_stale: home unprovisioned` | Add `--repair`. `curator run` always repairs. |
+| `profile_in_use` on remove | Run `curator profile use default` first. |
+| `env status --check` exits 1 on a healthy setup | Non-current profiles report `home unprovisioned`. Read the per-row findings rather than relying on the exit code. |
+| `security_posture_permissive` warning on every command | Set `"security_posture": "hardened"` in `~/.curator/config.json` if your policy allows it. |
+| Claude asks to log in inside `curator run` on macOS | Expected: the per-home Keychain item. Log in once for each managed home. |
+| `subcommand_provider_untrusted` | Move `curator-run` out of `~/.local/bin` or the managed directories. |
+
+## Unverified
+
+- Real `claude`/`codex` sessions. Only stubs were run, so the per-home
+  Keychain behaviour comes from registry facts verified on Claude 2.1.261,
+  not from a login.
+- Linux: the Claude `.credentials.json` link was not exercised.
+- The Codex `keyring` store branch was read from the code but not run.
+- The release installer (network download plus attestation) was not run.
